# Cloudflare Pages headers.
#
# The ITU coefficient files are the only genuinely immutable artifacts on this
# site: a given month's data never changes once published, and they are ~11 MB,
# so they are cached for a year. That is what keeps a repeat visit free of the
# download and keeps bandwidth cheap.
#
# Everything under vendor/ is BUILD OUTPUT and must revalidate.
#
# It did not, and that shipped a real bug. vendor/ looked immutable when it held
# only the compiled engine, so it carried a one-year `immutable` rule. Then the
# antenna model was added under vendor/ — and that changes on every deploy. A
# returning visitor's browser pinned a year-old copy while the HTML importing it
# updated around them, so the page loaded new markup against a stale module and
# quietly lost half its features. `immutable` means the browser does not even
# ask, so it does not heal on an ordinary reload.
#
# The rule now matches reality: without content-hashed filenames, build output
# revalidates. All of vendor/ is 640 KB, so the conditional requests that costs
# are a rounding error beside the 11 MB still cached hard.
#
# The same rule bit a second time, from an angle worth writing down: these
# patterns match the REQUEST PATH, not a file. While ionos09.bin was missing in
# September 2026 the host answered /data/itu/ionos09.bin with a 200 and the
# landing page — and this section stamped that HTML `immutable`, so every edge
# that was asked for the file while it was absent pinned an HTML page under a
# data URL for a year. Publishing the real file did not dislodge it; only a
# cache purge did. The checks that were meant to catch the outage were the
# requests that spread it.
#
# apps/web/404.html is what closes that: a missing path is now a 404, which
# Cloudflare returns `no-store` and does not cache at all. Keep it. Any future
# long-lived rule here should assume it will eventually be applied to a
# response for a file that is not there.

/vendor/*.wasm
  Content-Type: application/wasm

/vendor/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/data/itu/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/data/geo/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

# HTML always revalidates so a deploy is picked up immediately.
/*.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
